From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 14:52:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] stm32mp257-dk: expose RCC resources 50-51 to Linux

RCC resource 50 is the XBAR/flexgen resource backing ck_ker_fmc,
and resource 51 backs ck_ker_sdmmc1.
TF-A exposes it as non-secure, but OP-TEE's board RIF policy was
reapplying privileged/semaphore access before Linux booted.

Make only this resource non-privileged and semaphore-free so Linux can
touch the RCC register map while the migration away from OP-TEE-owned
firewall policy proceeds one resource at a time.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@local>
---
 core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp257f-dk-ca35tdcid-rif.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp257f-dk-ca35tdcid-rif.dtsi b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp257f-dk-ca35tdcid-rif.dtsi
index 6b575ba31..be570854 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp257f-dk-ca35tdcid-rif.dtsi
+++ b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp257f-dk-ca35tdcid-rif.dtsi
@@ -756,4 +756,4 @@
-		RIFPROT(RIF_RCC_RESOURCE(50), EMPTY_SEMWL, RIF_UNLOCK, RIF_NSEC, RIF_PRIV, RIF_UNUSED, RIF_SEM_EN, RIF_CFEN)
-		RIFPROT(RIF_RCC_RESOURCE(51), RIF_UNUSED, RIF_UNLOCK, RIF_SEC, RIF_PRIV, RIF_CID1, RIF_SEM_DIS, RIF_CFEN)
+		RIFPROT(RIF_RCC_RESOURCE(50), RIF_UNUSED, RIF_UNLOCK, RIF_NSEC, RIF_NPRIV, RIF_UNUSED, RIF_SEM_DIS, RIF_CFDIS)
+		RIFPROT(RIF_RCC_RESOURCE(51), RIF_UNUSED, RIF_UNLOCK, RIF_NSEC, RIF_NPRIV, RIF_UNUSED, RIF_SEM_DIS, RIF_CFDIS)
 		RIFPROT(RIF_RCC_RESOURCE(52), RIF_UNUSED, RIF_UNLOCK, RIF_SEC, RIF_PRIV, RIF_CID1, RIF_SEM_DIS, RIF_CFEN)
 		RIFPROT(RIF_RCC_RESOURCE(53), RIF_UNUSED, RIF_UNLOCK, RIF_SEC, RIF_PRIV, RIF_CID1, RIF_SEM_DIS, RIF_CFEN)
-- 
